# Line endings
#
# fix-white-icons.bat MUST be checked out with CRLF: cmd.exe's parser needs CRLF
# to resolve labels, and a copy checked out with LF-only endings fails at run
# time with "The system cannot find the batch label specified". Pinning it here
# makes that reliable no matter which platform the repository is cloned on.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Windows PowerShell scripts are conventionally CRLF as well.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Everything else is normalised to LF in the repository.
*.md   text
*.txt  text
*.json text
*.yml  text
*.yaml text

# Binary assets (screenshots for the README, for example) are never converted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
